        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): time out response body reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Browser response body capture could hang past its timeout when Playwright matched the response headers but the response body read never completed.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe response-body path now carries the existing response deadline through the Playwright `response.body()` read instead of clearing the timer after the matching response event. This keeps the existing URL matching and body truncation behavior while preventing a stalled body read from holding the tool call indefinitely.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers and automation that wait for a Browser response body now get a bounded timeout failure instead of a stuck command when the response body never resolves.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `b6db6b780110628e9d6d379b44b642983e05926e`.\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/browser/src/browser/pw-tools-core.responses.test.ts` passed on the PR head: 1 file, 2 tests, including the matched-response body timeout case.",
